// The **HTML** screen's two panes, under the header `HtmlChapter` puts over
// them: the Markdown screen's document with one node name changed.
//
// `text-area` writes `html.source`; `html-view` reads the same property with
// `bind=`. The element holding the preview is subscribed to the property, a
// keystroke marks it for rebuild, and the next frame is the parsed page. A live
// preview is a binding, whatever the document is written in.
//
// `link=` is the half that has no Markdown equivalent. An anchor in the page
// becomes a `button.link`, and pressing one calls this valued action with the
// `href`: what following a link means stays the application's.
//
// `html-view` is found the way `markdown-view` is: `goldberry-html`'s catalog
// declares the node name, and the inflater finds it on the module path.
split-pane id="html-split" position=0.5 first-min=240 second-min=240 {
    column id="html-editor" class="markdown-pane" {
        text class="caption" "HTML — type here"
        text-area id="html-source" class="mono" bind="html.source" change="html.set-source" fill=#true
    }
    column id="html-preview" class="markdown-pane" {
        text class="caption" "Rendered — this side follows"
        // What the last pressed link handed over: the toolkit hands over an
        // href and stops.
        text id="html-followed" class="caption" bind="html.followed"
        scroll {
            html-view id="html-rendered" bind="html.source" link="html.follow" images="app.assets"
        }
    }
}
